Z||000000||AusFiero||11-28-2001||06:19 PM||||Well ok thats a corny line out of an airline ad over here. But I am going to claim my birthday present now. Going to do some flying. Ok its only a Cessna I get to fly but I like it. Prices have dropped enough for me to get the license now&gt; up till now I just go on training flights. Take off, fly but no landing allowed.<P>Should be top fun, again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000001||JSocha||11-28-2001||06:21 PM||||Was that your big B-day present?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000002||rogergarrison||11-28-2001||07:17 PM||||I havent flown my plane in a while, fuels too expensive to go out for joyride by myself, everyone I knows chicken about flying in anything. I guess its because I like going low (legal altitude) and fast. Its no fun at 10,000 ft, seems like your just setting there. now at 1500 ft, now thats a blast.||||reg||1
Z||000003||California Kid||11-28-2001||07:51 PM||||Good for you Jim!! Have a lot of fun!<P>Roger, I know exactly what you're talking about, been there done that, illegal flying is the best!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever3000||11-28-2001||08:01 PM||||I'll fly with anybody, anytime!!!  Don't know why I never pursued a license, I love being in the air.  Once for my birthday, my wife chartered us a helicopter ride cause she knew I'd never flown in one before.  We took one of those bubble-shaped ones, for better picture-taking.  Was a blast.  <P>My 2 boys were in Civil Air Patrol for less than a year, and enjoyed it, but for some reason they dropped out of it.  The oldest one now says he wants to get back into it.<P>Enough about me, have a good flight Jim!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||AusFiero||11-28-2001||08:33 PM||||Woohoo. I was allowed to land the plane this time too. So I did it all. Just not long enough  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Well maybe next time I will go longer.<BR>To answer an earlier question ,yes, that was part of my Birthday present.<BR>Hmm So you have a plane hey Roger? I will be in the USA around the time of Dells next year. Need someone to pitch in for some fuel?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||11-29-2001||02:35 AM||||its a 77 Cessna XP. There a little rare because its a factory hotrod. It uses a IO 360, 6 cyl fuel injected, constant speed prop in a 172 airframe. Normally they have a carbed 4 cyl. it will almost climb straight up like a helo. You can throttle it up and pull back and it will almost stop mid air and keep flying.||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||11-29-2001||02:53 AM||||Woah!  Cool guys!<P>I've been totally hooked since before I could walk, I love flying!<P>Roger: how does 300 feet at 400knots sound? (even with TFR, it's *TERRIFYING*)<P>Woah! you have an XP!! (!!!)  Friend of mine is a profesional pilot, he's *green* with envy!   <P>We need to start a Fiero pilots club, so we can split gas costs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>its a 77 Cessna XP. There a little rare because its a factory hotrod. It uses a IO 360, 6 cyl fuel injected, constant speed prop in a 172 airframe. Normally they have a carbed 4 cyl. it will almost climb straight up like a helo. You can throttle it up and pull back and it will almost stop mid air and keep flying.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||11-29-2001||07:23 AM||||how a about 1200 mph at 100 feet...flew F4D Phantoms in Air Force in VN.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.........now thats adrenalin!||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||11-29-2001||08:07 AM||||heres a pic of it with my Mustang<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/my_172_Hawk_XP.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||WampusCat||11-29-2001||08:34 AM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>how a about 1200 mph at 100 feet...flew F4D Phantoms in Air Force in VN.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.........now thats adrenalin!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What was that, a secret nuclear powered F4D?  The phantoms were fast but 1200 mph(1043kts) at sea level?  I think not(unless pulling out of a long dive.) Sure at 40,000' it could go that fast but at sea level I think the top end was more like M1.2 or about 825 mph(aprox.720kts)  Over 700 kts down low is still freakin' fast though!!!  The fastest I ever got an AV-8B down low was 550 kts(630 mph).  Never busted that sound barrier thingy.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/icon9.gif">    <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/harrier_1.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by WampusCat (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||rogergarrison||11-29-2001||10:15 AM||||so I exaggerated a little, LOL. So you fly AV8s? Bet that wierd landing, dont know if id have the nerve for that, I even hate helicopters. and that was a ton of years ago to remember,   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. we did do a lot of high dives to deliver napalm at WOT.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula88||11-29-2001||10:47 AM||||Ok, I never flew myself, but I've been on some fun rides.  I took a ride with one of our local news helicopter pilots.  He learned to fly Huey's in 'nam, and showed me some of the "evasive" maneuvers he learned.  Scared me sh!tless!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>When I get my pilot's liscense, I want a Mooney TLS, but that's just a pipe dream right now.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Someday.  ||||reg||6
Z||000013||WampusCat||11-29-2001||10:49 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>so I exaggerated a little, LOL. So you fly AV8s?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not anymore...left the 'Corps in '96.  I was a TA-4 instructor in Kingsville, TX during Desert Storm, so the only napalm I ever dropped was in southern California.  Curently a first officer on the A320/319 so I don't really fly anymore, I just watch the "magic bus" do everything.  Well, I do fly a '46 Champ that belongs to our local EAA chapter on my days off.  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Phantom.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by WampusCat (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||rogergarrison||11-29-2001||12:36 PM||||I love that 5000th Phantom, cool paint job, I seen it before. Taylors are cool, I have a friend about 30 miles away with one. on a windy day it will fly backwards, lol. he used to fly over to Pt Columbus to visit. The control tower 'asked' him to refrain from hovering along the taxi ways, prefered he kept it on the pavement <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Another guy I knew had as S2B Pitts special he flew in local airshows. He had a heart attack in Lancaster, Oh during a loop and went straight into the ground. Aus, for your next birthday, You should get everyone to chip in to get a military jet ride!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||AusFiero||11-29-2001||03:21 PM||||Oh Yeah, that would be cool. Would be much more of a buzz than doing 90 knots in a cessna at 1500 feet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I am thinking about getting my pilots license. Costs about $6000 for a basic non commercial license. Could be worth it for some fun. <BR>The speeds you guys are talking hehehe. I was just happy to land the plane this time. They usually take over.||||reg||1
Z||000016||recluse||11-29-2001||11:49 PM||||I hope to get my pilots license someday, hopefully soon.  Heres the first (and only so far) cessna I've flown.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/plane1.jpg">   ||||reg||14
Z||000017||rogergarrison||11-30-2001||06:00 AM||||Hey recluse. I flew into Rockingham for the Nascar race before. They use the adjoining drag strip for a makeshift airport. that was strange landing between lite poles and trees. we all parked in the staging area, and air traffic control was a ANG C130 orbiting the speedway.<P>Aus, for your next bday you need to go to one of those 'Top Gun' places where you fly a couple of old AF training prop planes in simulated combat. A friend of mine had a blast. If your laser hits the opponent it sets off a smoke generator.||||reg||1
